{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. This is a prior-only model; no top-level data variable is observed/scored by a sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only sampling statement is the built-in prior `baseline ~ normal(0, 1);`, and there is no protected data interface to score.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;      // Number of observations

  // First factor information
  int<lower=0> N_factor1_levels;

  // Second factor information
  int<lower=0> N_factor2_levels;

  // Third factor information
  int<lower=0> N_factor3_levels;

  // Nesting configuration
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=N_factor3_levels> obs_to_factor3;
  array[N_factor3_levels] int<lower=1, upper=N_factor2_levels> factor3_to_factor2;
  array[N_factor2_levels] int<lower=1, upper=N_factor1_levels> factor2_to_factor1;
}

parameters {
  // Baseline
  real baseline;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[N_factor3_levels] log_psi = rep_vector(baseline, N_factor3_levels);
}

model {
  baseline ~ normal(0, 1);
}

","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 3,
  "N_factor1_levels": 1,
  "N_factor2_levels": 2,
  "N_factor3_levels": 2,
  "factor2_to_factor1": [
    1,
    1
  ],
  "factor3_to_factor2": [
    2,
    1
  ],
  "obs_to_factor3": [
    2,
    1,
    1
  ]
}
","protected_variables":[]}
